<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

<section id="Sx1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Note:</h5>

<div id="Sx1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We note that all figures and tables are presented after the body of the text due to their size.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1 </span>Human-Rated Dataset Creation and Generation Settings</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For human dataset creation, the models used are
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Sx1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[’mobius’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Corcelio 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’PixArt-Sigma-XL-2-1024-MS’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. 2024b</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’Juggernaut-XL-v8’
<br class="ltx_break"> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">RunDiffusion 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’RealVisXL_V4.0’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">SG161222 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’ProteusV0.4’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">dataautogpt3 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’Fluently-XL-v4’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">fluently 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’playground-v2.5-1024px-aesthetic’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’ColorfulXL-Lightning’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">recoilme and AiArtLab 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’colorfulxl’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">recoilme 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’stable-diffusion-v1-5’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">RunwayML 2022</a>)</cite>,
<br class="ltx_break">’sdxl-turbo’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sauer et al. 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’stable-diffusion-2-1’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al. 2021</a>)</cite>,
<br class="ltx_break">’stable-diffusion-2-base’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al. 2021</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’stable-diffusion-3-medium-diffusers’  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Esser et al. 2024</a>)</cite>, 
<br class="ltx_break">’stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0’ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Podell et al. 2023</a>)</cite>]</span>. 
<br class="ltx_break">Each of these models was run on the entire PartiPrompts dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al. 2022</a>)</cite>, at an image size of 1024x1024, 50 steps and guidance scale of 7.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Pairs of these images were then provided to raters via a Gradio survey, which is shown in <a href="#Sx1.F10" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. The raters consist of 40+ AI researchers who each rated on average 30 images.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2 </span>Task Definition and Reduction of Ambiguity</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the specific descriptions used of the tasks here. All were provided to both LLM and human annotators.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Sx1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Sx1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Aesthetic: “aesthetically better”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compositionality: “physical compositional (location/count) details of the prompt”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Style: “stylistic/color details”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Artifacts: “diffusiony sparkles or random unrendered parts of images, but deformed objects do not count.”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Anatomy: “better anatomy/object shape (e.g. no deformation or missing parts)”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="Sx1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Object Adherence: “relevant objects from the prompt”</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We believe that prompts disambiguate the various topics of the tasks, limiting concept confusion of annotators during the rating process. Human annotators were also instructed to list “Not relevant” whenever certain tasks were not present (like anatomy), which further serves to reduce concept confusion in the rating process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.3 </span>Sample Dataset Images</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional examples of annotations on diffusion generated images rated by humans in <a href="#Sx1.F11" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.4 </span>Synthetic Dataset Examples</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide additional examples from the synthetic datasets: aesthetic in <a href="#Sx1.F12" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, anatomy in <a href="#Sx1.F13" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, compositionality in <a href="#Sx1.F14" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, and style in <a href="#Sx1.F15" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.5 </span>Prompting Strategy</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the prompts used for evaluation and training for multi-image in <a href="#Sx1.F16" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, aesthetic and anatomy in <a href="#Sx1.F17" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, and compositionality and style in <a href="#Sx1.F18" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.6 </span>Model Training Ablations</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We sweep over a number of parameters. We sweep learning rate (5e-6 and 1e-5), number of training steps (200k, 400k, 800k), and a variety of data mixes over native LLaVA data, Commonalities and Differences (CaD) data, and our synthetic data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2023b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al. 2024a</a>)</cite>. We also train on the SynArtifact dataset for artifacts and Img-Diff dataset for object adherence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cao et al. 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiao et al. 2024</a>)</cite>. We evaluate the models on all validation datasets, and we find that our synthetic training paradigm on toy tasks does not generalize to the general multi-image rating task, which is expected due to the specialization of the toy datasets. We also find that training on other datasets does not transfer knowledge on a target task, with changes in accuracy being within noise. Detailed results can be found in: aesthetic toy dataset results in <a href="#Sx1.T4" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, anatomy toy dataset results in <a href="#Sx1.T5" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, compositionality toy dataset results in <a href="#Sx1.T6" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, style toy dataset results in <a href="#Sx1.T7" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, Cohen’s Kappa dataset results on the overall dataset in <a href="#Sx1.T8" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, and Pearson’s correlation coefficient results on the overall dataset in <a href="#Sx1.T9" title="In 8.6 Model Training Ablations ‣ Appendix ‣ What Makes a Good Generated Image? Investigating Human and Multimodal LLM Image Preference Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that models are named as
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Sx1.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[# samples]-[% llava data]-[% CaD data]-[% synthetic aesthetic data]-[% synthetic anatomy data]-[% SynArtifact data]-[% synthetic compositionality data]-[% Img-Diff data]-[% synthetic style data]-[learning rate]</span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
